 "schema_version": "1.0",
 "system": "Lal Kitab - a separate system, not part of the Parashari knowledge base",
 "sources": [
  "Pt. Roop Chand Joshi, Lal Kitab (1952 edition) as presented in widely used Lal Kitab references",
  "Pakka ghar, exalted / debilitated houses and good / weak houses: kept only where at least two Lal Kitab references agree; Rahu and Ketu vary between texts (see notes)",
  "Debts (rin): the nine classical debts. Each follows one rule: the enemies of a planet sitting in that planet's own Lal Kitab houses",
  "35-year cycle: Saturn 6, Rahu 6, Ketu 3, Jupiter 6, Sun 2, Moon 1, Venus 3, Mars 6, Mercury 2 (two references agree)",
  "Varshphal table (120 years): cross-checked row by row between two independent published copies (all 120 rows agree; a third copy agrees except for three rows with obvious typing errors) and against R. N. Bhandari's article (Saptarishis Astrology)"
 ],
 "notes": [
  "The Lal Kitab chart keeps every planet in the same house as the birth chart, but the signs are fixed: house 1 is always Aries, house 2 Taurus, and so on. Only house numbers matter.",
  "Texts differ for Rahu and Ketu: some give Ketu exalted in 9 and 12 and debilitated in 3 and 6, and Rahu debilitated in 9 and 12. The values here follow the more common reading.",
  "Lal Kitab remedies are traditional suggestions, never a cure or a guarantee. Remedies that harm animals, waste food or pollute water are left out on purpose."
 ],
